# upstream/82-clone-iterative: cloning a region keeps its place on an
# explicit stack, so its native depth does not grow with the IR's nesting,
# and the inliner and the compiler's copies keep a small stack. Operations
# nested 10,000 deep, each taking its block's argument, cloned on a thread
# whose stack is 256 KiB: every level is copied, and every operand of the
# copy is the copy's own argument (clone.cpp). The nesting is built in
# memory: mlir-opt's parser recurses on the same depth through each
# operation's parse hook, so through mlir-opt the clone is never seen alone.
# Building a program against MLIR's libraries takes longer than a step.
step_limit=180
. "$IDRIS_MLIR_ROOT/harness/testutils.sh"
mlir_check "clone: 10,000 nested operations on a 256 KiB stack, each operand mapped" "$here/clone.cpp" 10000
